1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,472
Here's what a fifteen-hundred-watt space heater costs per hour at full power, from cheapest state to priciest.

2
00:00:06,592 --> 00:00:08,599
Washington: about twenty-two cents.

3
00:00:08,719 --> 00:00:10,057
Florida: twenty-three.

4
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:11,409
Texas: twenty-four.

5
00:00:11,529 --> 00:00:13,026
Minnesota: twenty-five.

6
00:00:13,146 --> 00:00:16,230
The US average: about twenty-seven cents an hour.

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,009
New York: forty-four cents.

8
00:00:18,129 --> 00:00:19,900
Massachusetts: forty-five.

9
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,043
And California: about forty-nine cents an hour.

10
00:00:23,163 --> 00:00:25,072
Run it eight hours a day for a month,

11
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:30,833
and that's about fifty-two dollars in Washington, and about one hundred seventeen in California.

12
00:00:30,953 --> 00:00:32,318
Same heater, same heat.

13
00:00:32,438 --> 00:00:35,747
The only thing that changes is your electricity price.

14
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:40,167
So check your rate, then do the math for a fifteen-hundred-watt space heater…
